description:
FILED s518d (Opus 5.5, 2026-10-17) from #3284 (Path-Tiny t/filesystem.t and t/sig_die.t: "Error open (<) on '/tmp/XXXX'" after row 1).  SILENT WRONG, everyday shape, pre-existing (main 5c5a5679 alike).

A `my` declared in a `while` CONDITION is ONE variable across all iterations, so closures made in the body all see its LAST value (undef after the loop ends); perl gives each iteration its own.

REPRODUCER (scratch/s518d/pr/wh.pl):
    my %h = (a => 1, b => 2); my %s;
    while (my ($k, $v) = each %h) { $s{$k} = sub { $v } }
    my @l = (3, 4); my @t;
    while (my $x = shift @l) { push @t, sub { $x } }
    print join(",", map { "$_=" . $s{$_}->() } sort keys %s), " ", join(",", map { $_->() } @t), "\n";
perl 5.40.3: `a=1,b=2 3,4`.  PCL: `a=,b= ,`.

WHERE IT BITES: Path::Tiny builds openr/openw/opena/openrw (and their _raw/_utf8 variants) in `while ( my ( $k, $v ) = each %opens ) { *{$k} = sub { ... $v ... } }`, so every `->openw` opens with mode undef -> "<" and dies "Error open (<)" -- Path-Tiny filesystem.t (perl 108 rows) and sig_die.t (perl 4) stop after row 1.
Fix area: the loop-HEAD `my` (#297 gave it its own `let`); the let must be re-entered per iteration when a closure in the body captures it -- the foreach per-iteration binding is the sibling to reuse (rule 11).  For a scoping change the full sweep IS the gate.


=== DONE (s519a) ===
Commit 471b70c1 (m1).  Parser2 while/until: `_cond_mys_closure_captured` (scalar condition mys an anon sub in the body / continue block captures, via _block_captures_name); for those the test is `(progn (setf $x (make-p-box nil)) COND)` and the body + continue block are wrapped in `(p-let (($x :box $x)) ...)`.  Other loops: emission unchanged (corpus-diff vs fca3593b: the same 7 files as #3370, nothing from this member).  C-style for unchanged (perl: one variable).
BAR: the reproducer = perl (`a=1,b=2 3,4`); Pl/t/while-my-closure-01.t 4 rows (next/last/continue/redo, until, nested, two mys, C-for + no-closure counter-cases), 3 fail on fca3593b; Path-Tiny t/filesystem.t 1 -> 38 rows (stops at `subtest`, #1576; fails 11 = #2006 PART 2, 15-16 = #3412, 17 = #3413), t/sig_die.t 1 -> 3 of 4 (#2006 PART 2: the ->openw handle is not flushed at its block exit); the two *PLAN* rows citing #3374 left the board file by edit.  #300 (the same divergence, filed s385) folded here.
